1
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:42,240
After Phakorn recovers from surgery,

2
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:45,200
I'll send him to study in America.

3
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:48,040
I just want to say,
don't come to my house again.

4
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:50,440
Your aunt might get upset
and blame my mother again.

5
00:02:50,520 --> 00:02:52,880
This is Phakorn, my son.

6
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,840
I talked to Mr. Nimit

7
00:02:54,920 --> 00:02:57,320
about sending you to study in America.

8
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:59,440
And Alyssa is going there too.

9
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:02,520
<i>Since you'll be in the same place,</i>
<i>you can look out for each other.</i>

10
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:12,360
This is your office, Mr. Phakorn.

11
00:03:12,440 --> 00:03:14,520
You'll be responsible for brand strategy

12
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:17,720
as the Vice President of Brand Strategy.

13
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:23,440
Come in.

14
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:51,160
Whose car is that?

15
00:04:17,279 --> 00:04:18,480
Rawee!

16
00:04:20,279 --> 00:04:23,040
-Did you get the fish sauce for your mom?
-Yes.

17
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:13,120
Here you go.

18
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,880
Has Wee left yet, Phit?

19
00:05:14,960 --> 00:05:16,840
He just left a moment ago.

20
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,120
-Okay.
-Alright.

21
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:19,800
I was going to ask him
to get me some noodles.

22
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:37,640
Wee, could you get me some wonton soup?

23
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,040
I'm craving it.

24
00:05:40,280 --> 00:05:43,840
And get one for Somphit too.
The same as mine.

25
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,160
Sure.

26
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:02,080
CURRY PASTE - FRESH COCONUT MILK

27
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:06,720
The guy who eats less spicy dry noodles
hasn't been around lately.

28
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:09,440
He'll probably be back soon.

29
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,480
When he does, tell him to come see me.
I miss him.

30
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,960
I will, Auntie.

31
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:31,920
Korn.

32
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,440
When did you come back?

33
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:52,200
Have you been back for long?

34
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,480
You never even contacted me.

35
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:58,240
Not too long.

36
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:02,160
I've just been busy with things
at home and at the company.

37
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,240
Are you free today?

38
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,680
Let's go see Mom together.

39
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,720
Mom asks about you every day.

40
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:14,080
Maybe not today.
I'll go back when I get the chance.

41
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,280
Is something wrong, Korn?

42
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:22,600
Are you feeling sick?

43
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,920
Why do you look so pale?

44
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:29,320
Nothing's wrong with me.
I'm always this pale.

45
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:33,400
Oh, have you gotten fairer?

46
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,840
Wee, don't tell Mom we met yet.

47
00:07:42,360 --> 00:07:43,680
I have to get back to work.

48
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:50,440
By the way,

49
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:52,440
why are you here?

50
00:08:18,120 --> 00:08:19,240
Guess who?

51
00:08:19,320 --> 00:08:20,440
Alyssa.

52
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,600
I've missed you more than anything, Dad.

53
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:27,560
I've missed you too, sweetheart.

54
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:11,520
ALYSSA

55
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:13,720
ALYSSA

56
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,560
Hello.

57
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:18,000
I heard you're back. Is that true?

58
00:09:18,080 --> 00:09:19,840
<i>I just arrived yesterday.</i>

59
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,320
But you didn't even call?

60
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,480
Did you talk to my mother
without telling me?

61
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:28,600
It was about work.

62
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:30,840
That's how I found out you were back.

63
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:34,920
Then why did you call?

64
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:36,440
Do you miss me?

65
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:42,040
Yes, I miss you.
Your friends miss you too.

66
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:44,800
My friends?

67
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:47,520
You came back and didn't contact anyone.

68
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:49,640
Did you know they're having a party?

69
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:54,800
I know. Are you going?

70
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,120
Yes.

71
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,360
Don't forget my project launch event.

72
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:11,200
I'm already going as a partner.

73
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,800
Your mother hasn't told you yet, right?

74
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:16,720
I'm now a partner of Tayawat Group.

75
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:37,120
My name is Taddao.
I'm Ms. Nada's secretary.

76
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:39,400
I'll be training you as well, Rawee.

77
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,560
Thank you very much.

78
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:42,800
You came at the perfect time.

79
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:45,720
The company is about to launch
a new project,

80
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:47,720
so things
have been especially busy lately.

81
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:50,720
What kind of project is it?

82
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:54,440
A retirement condo. For the rich.

83
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,120
We could never afford it.

84
00:10:57,880 --> 00:10:58,800
We're here.

85
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:01,200
Let's go.

86
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:07,840
This way, Rawee.

87
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:15,360
Hello.

88
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:19,400
Have a seat, Rawee.

89
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:20,800
Thank you.

90
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:28,280
How is your mother? Is she doing well?

91
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,360
She's doing well.

92
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:33,720
I'm really happy

93
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,160
that you came to help us here.

94
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:39,640
Learn the job from Taddao first,

95
00:11:39,720 --> 00:11:41,320
then you can come help me.

96
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:43,760
Yes.

97
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:48,160
Have you met Korn yet?

98
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:53,800
Wee, don't tell Mom we met yet.

99
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,360
Not yet.

100
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:02,880
That's okay. Once you work here,

101
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:04,520
you'll see him every day.

102
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:07,920
Yes.

103
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,040
Dad.

104
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:26,600
I'd like to start our joint project
with Tayawat now.

105
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:28,680
I talked to Aunt Nada.
Everything went well.

106
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:32,600
What is this, dear? You just graduated.
Aren't you going to take a break first?

107
00:12:32,680 --> 00:12:34,400
Why are you so fired up?

108
00:12:35,040 --> 00:12:36,360
I'm not tired at all.

109
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:39,160
Tayawat is also launching a new project.

110
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:41,200
I think this is
the best opportunity right now.

111
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:44,800
Go ahead.
If you think it's good, then do it.

112
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:47,640
Actually, Nada and I
have known each other for a long time.

113
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:50,520
I never thought we'd end up
becoming business partners.

114
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:54,000
If you have a path forward,
that's a good thing.

115
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,160
I fully support you.

116
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:57,640
Thank you.

117
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:06,720
By the way…

118
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:12,360
Has Uncle Jak
been causing any more trouble?

119
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:15,160
Don't you trust your dad?

120
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:18,840
If I say I'll handle it, I'll handle it.

121
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:22,440
If I really get serious,
no one will dare oppose me.

122
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,760
-There is one person.
-Huh?

123
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:26,920
Your daughter.

124
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:37,880
Are Aunt Walai and her son
still working at the factory?

125
00:13:38,680 --> 00:13:41,320
Yes, they are. But Nada

126
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,080
has recruited Rawee away.

127
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,440
He really hit the jackpot.

128
00:13:46,480 --> 00:13:47,520
Aunt Pat.

129
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:56,320
Sorry. It just slipped out.

130
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:01,240
Walai is still selling food, though.

131
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:04,280
I'm taking good care of those two
like you asked.

132
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:05,440
Don't worry.

133
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:08,280
Okay.

134
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,160
Alyssa.

135
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:18,040
You're close with Nada's son, right?

136
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,240
Can I get his number?

137
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:25,960
Sure.
What do you need Korn's number for, Dad?

138
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:38,880
Hello.

139
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:47,120
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

140
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,880
-What can I get you?
-Hello.

141
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:53,120
Hello.

142
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:55,280
It's Alyssa.

143
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:58,040
Oh, Alyssa!

144
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:01,440
You're so beautiful,
I almost didn't recognize you.

145
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,720
You've already graduated and came back?

146
00:15:03,800 --> 00:15:04,640
Yes.

147
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:08,200
I really have to thank your father

148
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:10,280
for helping me make a living.

149
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:12,720
Your cooking is delicious too, Auntie.

150
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:22,440
Well, Rawee isn't here.

151
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:26,160
He got a new job in Bangkok.
He has a lot to prepare.

152
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,200
I'm happy for him.

153
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:32,240
Yes. But he'll probably be here soon.

154
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:35,240
Once he finishes packing this afternoon,
he'll head to Bangkok.

155
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:37,080
Do you want to wait and see him?

156
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:41,960
I don't think
your son would want to see me.

157
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,800
Why would you say that?

158
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:47,080
Wee is actually a very kind person.

159
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:52,520
I think I'll have lunch here.

160
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:54,520
Of course.

161
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:56,040
Let me get you some rice.

162
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:57,200
What would you like?

163
00:15:58,880 --> 00:16:01,360
-I'll have egg and pork stew, please.
-Alright.

164
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:02,520
Egg and pork stew.

165
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:30,560
Oh, has Mom already gone to work?

166
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:33,440
Yes.
Would you like breakfast now, Mr. Korn?

167
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:34,440
Yeah.

168
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:54,040
Why did you come to the meeting with me?
You should be resting at home.

169
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:56,800
I told you, Dad. I came back this time

170
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:59,400
ready to help you with the work.

171
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:00,680
I'm ready to work.

172
00:18:01,320 --> 00:18:02,640
With you working this hard,

173
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:05,240
I might be out of a job.

174
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:07,240
Better start preparing for retirement,
Mr. Nimit.

175
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:09,560
See? I knew it.

176
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:11,440
Wait here for me a moment.

177
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,440
Of course.

178
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:32,480
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

179
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:36,040
Whoa, this is so refreshing.

180
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:39,080
-Let me try some first.
-Hey, Korn.

181
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:42,480
Have you changed your last name
to Tayawat yet?

182
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:47,440
Not yet. Since I came back,
Mom's been busy all the time.

183
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:49,960
Are you sure you're really his son?

184
00:18:50,560 --> 00:18:52,760
What if your dad was sleeping around,

185
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:56,640
and when your mom found out you weren't
her son, she kept putting it off?

186
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:58,040
Why don't you write a novel?

187
00:18:58,120 --> 00:18:59,400
Want one? I'll write it for you.

188
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,320
Huh?

189
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,520
Twenty years separated from your family,

190
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:07,080
with only a diary and a family ring
to prove you're her son.

191
00:19:07,160 --> 00:19:09,680
Your life is like a damn soap opera, Korn.

192
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:13,040
Hey, Korn. I'm serious.

193
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:16,720
I think you should hurry
and get your mom to handle this.

194
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:20,520
Right now, you're just some poor kid

195
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:23,200
who got a scholarship from her.
That's all.

196
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,320
Outsiders don't know you're her son.

197
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,840
But legally speaking,

198
00:19:29,920 --> 00:19:31,520
you're still a stranger right now.

199
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:34,040
He's right.

200
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,080
Let's dig in.

201
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:14,320
Wow, Wee. This house is so big.

202
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,560
Are you sure Mr. Nimit
is renting it out at this price?

203
00:20:17,160 --> 00:20:20,320
Yes. I think he just wants to help me.

204
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:24,400
I was thinking I'd pay him more
once I pass my probation.

205
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:25,720
I feel bad, Mom.

206
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:29,080
That's good, Son.
Let's bring the things inside.

207
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,240
-Yes.
-Come on.

208
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:12,480
This is Phakorn, Father.

209
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:15,800
Hello, Grandpa.

210
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:21,360
This is your uncle, Panas.

211
00:21:22,680 --> 00:21:23,520
Hello.

212
00:21:24,960 --> 00:21:27,960
And this is your aunt, Pimpa.

213
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:31,200
Hello.

214
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,440
I don't consider you family.

215
00:21:37,960 --> 00:21:39,280
Watch yourself.

216
00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:43,080
It's his first day
setting foot in this house.

217
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:46,040
Why are you so against Nada and her son?

218
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:49,160
You're still siblings, after all.

219
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:51,440
It's fine, Father.

220
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:55,640
Now that I know we're not family.

221
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,160
Then,

222
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:01,560
I won't have to respect you anymore.

223
00:22:03,040 --> 00:22:06,200
Come on, Nada. That was harsh.

224
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:08,280
Your sister started it.

225
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:09,840
What did I do wrong?

226
00:22:09,920 --> 00:22:12,200
He's still using a different surname.

227
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:14,280
Ugh.

228
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:17,040
When will you two stop fighting?

229
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:22,600
Bring my grandson closer to me.

230
00:22:24,360 --> 00:22:25,200
Come on, Son.

231
00:22:42,680 --> 00:22:44,560
When will you file the petition
with the court?

232
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:47,880
He's no longer a missing person.

233
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:51,520
Then he can finally use
our family name legally.

234
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:55,400
I've been busy lately.

235
00:22:55,920 --> 00:23:00,240
Let's wait until after the condo launch,
then we'll discuss it.

236
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:02,480
Do you want my lawyer to help?

237
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:05,080
That way,
we can get everything sorted out.

238
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:08,960
If I can clear my schedule,

239
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:11,000
I'll ask for your help, Father.

240
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,360
Where are you going?

241
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:23,840
To the bathroom.

242
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:27,040
Not yet. Sit and talk with us first.

243
00:23:36,400 --> 00:23:38,640
Don't think being the only grandson

244
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:42,600
gives you the right
to act arrogant like your mother.

245
00:23:45,280 --> 00:23:48,160
And the reason
we let your mother run the company

246
00:23:48,240 --> 00:23:50,120
was only because of Father.

247
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:51,600
Not because my mother

248
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:54,120
was capable enough to negotiate deals

249
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:56,720
and bring in foreign investors?

250
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:01,000
You sound just like your mother.

251
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:02,040
Enough, Pim.

252
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:05,200
The kid just hit a nerve,

253
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:06,880
and you're already worked up.

254
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:08,280
Panas!

255
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,920
I'm not the one with issues.

256
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,160
Your mother is.

257
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:21,880
What issues?

258
00:24:24,440 --> 00:24:26,080
Don't tell me you still don't know

259
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:28,600
that your mother

260
00:24:28,680 --> 00:24:30,600
was the daughter of a mistress.

261
00:24:32,160 --> 00:24:34,680
And she was even a servant in this house.

262
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:41,000
Now that you know the truth, stay humble.

263
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:43,280
Maybe people will still be kind to you.

264
00:24:44,680 --> 00:24:46,720
-And don't say--
-Enough, Pim.

265
00:24:47,880 --> 00:24:49,840
You're like a villain
fighting over an inheritance.

266
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:52,280
No matter what, Korn is still our nephew.

267
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:54,680
Forget it, Panas.

268
00:24:55,280 --> 00:24:58,280
If she insults me, I'll insult her back.
That's only fair.

269
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:02,720
So arrogant. Both mother and Son.

270
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:06,880
I'm confident
because I have something to back it up.

271
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:09,520
Not the kind of confidence

272
00:25:09,600 --> 00:25:12,760
that keeps causing
company projects to fail.

273
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:16,760
Da.

274
00:25:17,360 --> 00:25:19,320
I'll take him outside for a bit.

275
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:21,640
He'll be able to breathe a little easier.

276
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:24,120
Let's go, Korn.

277
00:25:41,560 --> 00:25:42,480
Wee.

278
00:25:43,480 --> 00:25:45,120
Are you hiding something from me?

279
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:47,640
What did you hear, Mom?

280
00:25:49,280 --> 00:25:51,800
Do you know that Korn is back?

281
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:54,760
How did you find out?

282
00:25:57,040 --> 00:25:59,680
I talked to Mr. Nimit this morning.

283
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:02,760
Why? Did you already know?

284
00:26:05,120 --> 00:26:08,120
No. I was just surprised.

285
00:26:08,200 --> 00:26:10,880
I wondered why Korn hadn't contacted me.

286
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:15,880
Maybe he's planning a surprise for us.

287
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:18,040
He's always been a prankster.

288
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:22,280
I wonder if he'll still be the same.

289
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,440
Why wouldn't he be?

290
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:30,960
I don't know
what hardships he's been through.

291
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:33,960
I pray every day that I made

292
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,760
the right choice in sending Korn away.

293
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:37,760
As long as he got treatment

294
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:39,880
and came back alive,

295
00:26:39,960 --> 00:26:42,400
it means you made the right choice.

296
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:44,120
You don't have to worry.

297
00:26:45,120 --> 00:26:46,400
By the way,

298
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,600
Wee.

299
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:52,280
When you see your brother,
please treat him the same as before.

300
00:26:57,840 --> 00:27:00,840
Why are older people
so worried all the time?

301
00:27:03,320 --> 00:27:04,600
Korn and I

302
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,480
grew up together.

303
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:09,760
A little time apart won't change us.

304
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:12,440
Once we see each other,

305
00:27:12,520 --> 00:27:16,360
we'll be close again in no time. Trust me.

306
00:27:18,560 --> 00:27:20,360
Okay. Oh, hey.

307
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:23,240
Wee, Mr. Nimit gave me Korn's number.

308
00:27:23,320 --> 00:27:26,320
I was thinking of calling him.
Do you think I should?

309
00:27:28,840 --> 00:27:30,200
Alright.

310
00:27:42,760 --> 00:27:43,600
Hey.

311
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:48,080
Wait here for a moment.
I'll get you something to drink.

312
00:27:49,120 --> 00:27:50,160
Thank you.

313
00:27:50,680 --> 00:27:51,920
Make yourself comfortable.

314
00:28:33,120 --> 00:28:34,560
Hello.

315
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:36,720
<i>Korn? Is this Korn?</i>

316
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:38,840
<i>It's me, Mom. Do you remember me?</i>

317
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:43,400
Mom. Where did you get my number?

318
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:46,520
You're back, aren't you, Korn?

319
00:28:47,120 --> 00:28:49,440
Yes. I'm back.

320
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:53,760
Why didn't you come see me?
Even a call would've been nice.

321
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:56,720
Wee is here with me too.
Do you want to talk to him?

322
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:03,440
I…

323
00:29:07,880 --> 00:29:09,160
Oh?

324
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:21,840
Thank you.

325
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:26,840
Are you talking to your old family?
Why don't you keep talking?

326
00:29:27,600 --> 00:29:30,520
Well…

327
00:29:30,600 --> 00:29:32,640
I was planning to surprise them.

328
00:29:35,120 --> 00:29:38,520
So you haven't been back
to your old home since you returned?

329
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:42,760
No. I haven't had the time yet.

330
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,560
Let's go eat.

331
00:30:03,880 --> 00:30:06,840
Don't let anyone look down on us, Korn.

332
00:30:08,840 --> 00:30:10,560
But what can I do, Mom?

333
00:30:11,520 --> 00:30:15,160
If we show weakness,
we'll lose everything.

334
00:30:15,800 --> 00:30:18,000
You have to defeat everyone

335
00:30:18,640 --> 00:30:20,720
with your own ability, like I did.

336
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:26,600
Yes, Mother.

337
00:30:32,680 --> 00:30:34,720
I'm not jealous, Father.

338
00:30:35,600 --> 00:30:37,480
I'm just saying what's obvious.

339
00:30:37,560 --> 00:30:39,040
No matter how I look at it,

340
00:30:39,120 --> 00:30:42,200
Phakorn is nothing like Nada or Rawich.

341
00:30:43,480 --> 00:30:45,440
Either Nada deceived us,

342
00:30:45,520 --> 00:30:48,520
or Nada herself
was deceived by that family.

343
00:30:51,360 --> 00:30:53,480
I won't deny that the ring is real.

344
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:56,800
And Nada's diary is real too.

345
00:30:57,480 --> 00:31:00,200
But people can fake things, Father.

346
00:31:03,040 --> 00:31:05,000
Nada herself is suspicious.

347
00:31:05,080 --> 00:31:08,520
She keeps refusing to take a DNA test.

348
00:31:10,920 --> 00:31:13,280
Your grandson might already be dead,

349
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:15,560
and someone else may have taken his place.

350
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:17,520
Don't get worked up.

351
00:31:18,800 --> 00:31:21,200
Without a clear DNA test,

352
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:24,400
I'm not stupid enough
to accept him as my grandson.

353
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:29,240
Perfect timing. The food's already cold.

354
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:30,920
Sit next to me.

355
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:47,760
What a happy family.

356
00:31:48,600 --> 00:31:50,320
What family are you talking about?

357
00:31:52,400 --> 00:31:53,240
I forgot.

358
00:31:54,040 --> 00:31:56,680
Your husband left you,
so you wouldn't understand.

359
00:31:57,360 --> 00:31:59,240
Even though I'm single,
I still understand it.

360
00:31:59,320 --> 00:32:01,400
Panas!

361
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:02,680
Hey.

362
00:32:02,760 --> 00:32:04,600
A lady doesn't address people that way.

363
00:32:05,520 --> 00:32:06,600
Hey.

364
00:32:06,680 --> 00:32:08,880
When will you two stop fighting?

365
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:16,240
Come on, eat.

366
00:32:48,680 --> 00:32:50,160
What is it, Korn?

367
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:52,680
Have you told anyone the truth, Wee?

368
00:32:54,520 --> 00:32:55,400
What truth?

369
00:32:55,480 --> 00:32:57,640
About the two of us switching places.

370
00:32:59,080 --> 00:33:00,080
Why would you tell them?

371
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:02,400
What about Mom?

372
00:33:03,000 --> 00:33:04,120
Especially not Mom.

373
00:33:06,160 --> 00:33:08,880
Why are you suddenly asking about this?

374
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:15,400
I still haven't changed
my surname to Tayawat.

375
00:33:16,840 --> 00:33:19,760
Mom still won't get the paperwork done.

376
00:33:19,840 --> 00:33:22,360
She's rich enough
to speed things up if she wanted.

377
00:33:25,080 --> 00:33:28,480
There's only one reason
she won't finish it.

378
00:33:29,080 --> 00:33:31,280
She knows I'm not her real son.

379
00:33:32,040 --> 00:33:34,920
If they don't accept you,
we can just keep living like this, Korn.

380
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:37,560
You're healthy now.
You graduated overseas.

381
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:39,520
You've gained so much already.
What more do you want?

382
00:33:39,600 --> 00:33:42,200
I've come too far, Wee. I can't go back…

383
00:33:46,840 --> 00:33:49,480
Or do you want your place as her son back?

384
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:52,160
Why would you say that?

385
00:33:59,120 --> 00:33:59,960
Korn.

386
00:34:01,280 --> 00:34:02,600
Go see Mom sometime.

387
00:34:03,240 --> 00:34:04,600
She misses you so much.

388
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:10,600
Is something wrong, Son?

389
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:16,640
Mom.

390
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:19,800
Can we go to court
and get everything done this week?

391
00:35:21,360 --> 00:35:25,440
I just want to use
the Tayawat surname like you.

392
00:35:25,520 --> 00:35:29,160
Then my aunt and uncle
won't look down on me anymore.

393
00:35:30,480 --> 00:35:33,160
Can we wait
until after the condo launch event?

394
00:35:33,240 --> 00:35:34,680
I'm very busy right now.

395
00:35:40,520 --> 00:35:42,800
There are a lot of documents
we need to prepare.

396
00:35:43,600 --> 00:35:47,040
Right now, your personal records

397
00:35:47,800 --> 00:35:50,480
still identify you as someone else,
not my son.

398
00:35:51,600 --> 00:35:53,200
The court might think

399
00:35:54,400 --> 00:35:55,440
you're impersonating

400
00:35:56,280 --> 00:35:58,240
someone who died.

401
00:36:03,560 --> 00:36:06,560
I see. Then

402
00:36:06,640 --> 00:36:08,920
it's better
to prepare everything properly.

403
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:11,000
Yes.

404
00:36:14,440 --> 00:36:15,640
Don't stay up too late.

405
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:17,880
Okay.

406
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,920
These are Phakorn's documents

407
00:36:51,200 --> 00:36:52,360
for his further studies.

408
00:36:54,120 --> 00:36:56,080
Mrs. Walai signed all the documents,
right?

409
00:36:56,680 --> 00:36:58,200
-Yes.
-Okay.

410
00:36:58,960 --> 00:37:02,120
Then there shouldn't be any problems.

411
00:37:02,840 --> 00:37:06,560
At first glance,
that seems to be the case.

412
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:12,800
But if you look closely at the evidence,
you'll see

413
00:37:13,520 --> 00:37:17,160
that Phakorn isn't an adopted child.
He's actually Walai's biological son.

414
00:37:18,840 --> 00:37:21,920
While your real son is Rawee.

415
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:30,560
Well…

416
00:37:30,640 --> 00:37:34,440
I already knew
the truth from Mrs. Walai's husband.

417
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:37,040
I'm sorry for hiding this from you.

418
00:37:37,800 --> 00:37:39,360
You mean

419
00:37:39,440 --> 00:37:42,320
Mrs. Walai intentionally switched Phakorn

420
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:44,400
so he could receive treatment?

421
00:37:44,480 --> 00:37:45,840
Yes.

422
00:37:46,520 --> 00:37:49,880
It seems Rawee agreed too,
because he loves his brother very much.

423
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:52,400
That's why I decided not to tell you

424
00:37:52,480 --> 00:37:54,760
until after Phakorn's surgery.

425
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:02,760
Think of it as repaying Mrs. Walai

426
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:04,920
for raising and taking care of Rawee
all these years.

427
00:38:12,280 --> 00:38:14,040
Now that we know the truth,

428
00:38:15,280 --> 00:38:16,600
what should we do next?

429
00:38:19,440 --> 00:38:20,440
Leave it as it is.

430
00:38:21,880 --> 00:38:23,120
Are you sure that's a good idea?

431
00:38:24,120 --> 00:38:27,520
The reason I sent Phakorn abroad
to study right away

432
00:38:27,600 --> 00:38:31,040
was because I feared
he would be in danger. Honestly,

433
00:38:31,120 --> 00:38:32,920
I never trusted Pim.

434
00:38:35,880 --> 00:38:37,040
Since

435
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:39,920
they switched places,

436
00:38:41,560 --> 00:38:43,320
Rawee is even safer.

437
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:48,480
But won't Rawee
lose his opportunities this way?

438
00:38:51,360 --> 00:38:53,000
Let him finish his studies first.

439
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:55,800
I'll bring him into the company to help.

440
00:38:55,880 --> 00:38:57,840
And I'll support him.

441
00:39:02,680 --> 00:39:05,800
What about Phakorn? Should we tell him?

442
00:39:18,160 --> 00:39:19,720
Wine, Mom.

443
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,920
Why didn't you let Maem bring it?

444
00:39:24,560 --> 00:39:27,000
I was just about to come in
and say good night.

445
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:31,040
Here you go.

446
00:39:31,720 --> 00:39:32,800
Thank you.

447
00:39:45,680 --> 00:39:46,520
Mom.

448
00:39:48,680 --> 00:39:51,000
So, about the evidence,

449
00:39:51,080 --> 00:39:53,480
do we need to go as far
as getting a DNA test?

450
00:39:56,440 --> 00:40:00,200
I'm not sure either. I'll ask the lawyer.

451
00:40:01,720 --> 00:40:04,440
If you can find someone
to speed things up, that'd be great.

452
00:40:04,520 --> 00:40:07,040
It may cost more, but it'll save time.

453
00:40:07,120 --> 00:40:08,680
It'll be less work for you too.

454
00:40:10,600 --> 00:40:13,880
That's true. I'll ask some friends.

455
00:40:15,720 --> 00:40:19,040
Good. Then I won't bother you anymore.

456
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:26,040
-Good night.
-Good night.

457
00:40:59,280 --> 00:41:00,680
I'll go pick you up.

458
00:41:21,160 --> 00:41:23,560
I heard Mr. Nimit
say someone rented this house.

459
00:41:23,640 --> 00:41:25,280
I never thought it would be you.

460
00:41:26,680 --> 00:41:29,160
You can actually afford
to rent a house this big?

461
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:33,280
Or does Mr. Nimit
let you stay here for free?

462
00:41:34,480 --> 00:41:35,960
Do you need something, Auntie?

463
00:41:36,040 --> 00:41:38,320
I'm not your aunt!

464
00:41:39,400 --> 00:41:40,280
Aunt Pat.

465
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:42,880
Weren't you bringing rice porridge
to the neighbors?

466
00:41:46,480 --> 00:41:47,360
I just found out

467
00:41:47,440 --> 00:41:50,800
that the person
renting your father's house is this guy.

468
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:54,840
That's not very nice.

469
00:41:54,920 --> 00:41:57,640
We don't know him well enough
to speak that way. He might be offended.

470
00:41:58,240 --> 00:42:01,200
-Alyssa!
-I'm sorry on my aunt's behalf.

471
00:42:14,440 --> 00:42:17,920
I just found out too
that my father rented this house to you.

472
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:21,280
Is there anything else you need from me?

473
00:42:21,840 --> 00:42:23,520
If not, I'll excuse myself.

474
00:42:24,160 --> 00:42:25,640
The rice porridge.

475
00:42:29,800 --> 00:42:32,320
Take it back.
I don't eat things from your aunt.

476
00:43:00,360 --> 00:43:01,840
-May we take some photos, Ms. Nada?
-Sure.

477
00:43:01,920 --> 00:43:02,960
Of course.

478
00:43:03,720 --> 00:43:05,280
Look at this camera, please.

479
00:43:05,360 --> 00:43:07,520
-Please look this way.
-This camera, please.

480
00:43:07,600 --> 00:43:09,800
This one too, please. Great. Beautiful.

481
00:43:09,880 --> 00:43:12,520
Please wait a moment for my son, Phakorn.

482
00:43:12,600 --> 00:43:13,840
Just a little more.

483
00:43:13,920 --> 00:43:15,080
-Smile, please.
-Beautiful.

484
00:43:15,160 --> 00:43:16,680
Ms. Nada, you look beautiful.

485
00:43:16,760 --> 00:43:17,600
Great.

486
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:24,280
-Mr. Phakorn has arrived.
-Go bring him here right away.

487
00:43:28,840 --> 00:43:30,800
Please invite everyone up onto the stage.

488
00:43:30,880 --> 00:43:31,880
Yes.

489
00:43:57,440 --> 00:44:00,520
Excuse me. Sorry.

490
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:05,880
Mr. Phakorn,
everyone inside is waiting for you.

491
00:44:05,960 --> 00:44:07,400
Okay.

492
00:44:07,480 --> 00:44:09,400
Excuse me. This way, please.

493
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:12,240
Please let us through.
Sorry. Excuse me. This way, please.

494
00:44:26,520 --> 00:44:28,480
-Smile, please.
-Look at the camera.

495
00:44:29,520 --> 00:44:31,440
-Great.
-Perfect.

496
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:33,400
-Good. Look at the camera.
-Hello.

497
00:44:33,480 --> 00:44:35,120
-Hello.
-Great.

498
00:44:35,200 --> 00:44:37,520
Hurry up. We're waiting for you.

499
00:44:39,360 --> 00:44:41,440
You have no sense of timing.

500
00:44:41,520 --> 00:44:42,920
Go stand next to Panas.

501
00:44:48,040 --> 00:44:49,880
Phakorn, stand next to me.

502
00:44:51,920 --> 00:44:54,560
Ready? This camera, please.

503
00:44:54,640 --> 00:44:56,280
Ready?

504
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:58,400
-This camera.
-Look at this camera, please.

505
00:44:58,480 --> 00:44:59,920
Great.

506
00:45:01,760 --> 00:45:04,240
I guess our stars must really align.

507
00:45:04,320 --> 00:45:07,120
After meeting once,
we keep running into each other.

508
00:45:08,960 --> 00:45:10,960
Hopefully not forever.

509
00:45:12,440 --> 00:45:14,440
Are you still upset about my aunt?

510
00:45:16,040 --> 00:45:17,080
I'm not upset.

511
00:45:18,480 --> 00:45:22,160
You're not upset,
but you do sound sarcastic.

512
00:45:27,840 --> 00:45:29,680
I'm sorry.

513
00:45:29,760 --> 00:45:31,320
can I ask…

514
00:45:32,880 --> 00:45:33,960
how your leg is doing?

515
00:45:35,560 --> 00:45:37,800
It may not be back to 100%,

516
00:45:37,880 --> 00:45:40,720
but it doesn't stop me
from living my life.

517
00:45:44,120 --> 00:45:47,440
Hearing that makes me feel much better.

518
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:51,000
You can stop feeling guilty now.

519
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:55,360
Your father has already helped my family
more than I could ever repay.

520
00:45:56,720 --> 00:45:58,280
Forget about this.

521
00:45:58,880 --> 00:46:00,520
Then does that mean

522
00:46:01,720 --> 00:46:03,760
we can be friends now?

523
00:46:08,880 --> 00:46:09,720
Yes?

524
00:46:11,280 --> 00:46:13,160
Yes, I'll be right there.

525
00:46:16,040 --> 00:46:17,720
I have to get back to work first.

526
00:46:25,840 --> 00:46:28,920
Hey, see that person over there?

527
00:46:29,000 --> 00:46:31,640
Yeah. That's Mr. Panas.

528
00:46:31,720 --> 00:46:35,480
The youngest son.
He gets an executive director's salary,

529
00:46:35,560 --> 00:46:37,680
but he never actually works.

530
00:46:37,760 --> 00:46:39,640
His only job is

531
00:46:39,720 --> 00:46:42,720
attending board meetings.
They keep him around to balance power.

532
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:45,840
He just votes however the chairman wants.

533
00:46:45,920 --> 00:46:46,800
That's all.

534
00:46:48,480 --> 00:46:51,480
Hey, another one. Over there.

535
00:46:52,280 --> 00:46:54,200
The one chatting and laughing?

536
00:46:54,280 --> 00:46:58,000
Yeah, that one. This woman

537
00:46:58,080 --> 00:47:01,960
is the toughest person in the company.
Stay away if you can.

538
00:47:02,040 --> 00:47:03,360
Got it?

539
00:47:03,960 --> 00:47:06,280
That's Ms. Pimpa,

540
00:47:06,360 --> 00:47:08,160
the eldest daughter.

541
00:47:08,240 --> 00:47:10,960
She was married, but she's divorced now.

542
00:47:11,040 --> 00:47:12,280
So now she's single

543
00:47:12,360 --> 00:47:14,560
and spends a lot of time at host bars.

544
00:47:14,640 --> 00:47:17,720
But believe it or not,

545
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:19,640
she still comes to the company every day.

546
00:47:19,720 --> 00:47:22,600
I don't even know
why she bothers coming in.

547
00:47:22,680 --> 00:47:24,760
She doesn't do any actual work.

548
00:47:25,680 --> 00:47:26,760
Oh!

549
00:47:26,840 --> 00:47:28,160
Recently,

550
00:47:28,240 --> 00:47:30,040
she was demoted

551
00:47:30,120 --> 00:47:33,040
from an executive position
to a department manager.

552
00:47:33,120 --> 00:47:35,960
Because she made mistakes.

553
00:47:36,040 --> 00:47:38,880
If she weren't the chairman's daughter,
she would've been fired.

554
00:47:38,960 --> 00:47:40,520
She is

555
00:47:40,600 --> 00:47:43,360
Ms. Nada's biggest rival.

556
00:47:43,440 --> 00:47:44,720
By the way,

557
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:46,800
Mr. Phakorn
is about to start working here.

558
00:47:46,880 --> 00:47:49,560
I wonder what kind of person he is.

559
00:47:51,560 --> 00:47:53,680
I think he seems like a good person.

560
00:47:54,200 --> 00:47:56,160
He looks sharp and intelligent.

561
00:47:57,800 --> 00:47:58,840
Sounds like you know him.

562
00:48:00,840 --> 00:48:04,760
I saw him earlier.
I happen to be able to read feng shui.

563
00:48:04,840 --> 00:48:06,360
You mean face reading?

564
00:48:06,440 --> 00:48:08,640
Oh, face reading. Yes.

565
00:48:20,400 --> 00:48:21,320
Here you go.

566
00:48:22,760 --> 00:48:23,560
Are you hungry?

567
00:48:24,280 --> 00:48:25,240
Not yet.

568
00:48:29,520 --> 00:48:30,520
Mom.

569
00:48:32,600 --> 00:48:34,920
There's someone I'd like you to meet.

570
00:48:37,280 --> 00:48:38,160
Here she is.

571
00:48:39,440 --> 00:48:40,360
Alyssa.

572
00:48:40,440 --> 00:48:41,640
Hello, Auntie.

573
00:48:41,720 --> 00:48:44,240
-Hello.
-This is my girlfriend.

574
00:48:48,720 --> 00:48:49,760
Then why don't you two get married?

575
00:48:55,960 --> 00:48:57,160
Oh, Rawee.

576
00:48:58,880 --> 00:48:59,960
Come here.

577
00:49:04,760 --> 00:49:06,120
Have you two met?

578
00:49:09,000 --> 00:49:12,000
Korn, I've hired Rawee to work with us.

579
00:49:13,720 --> 00:49:14,880
We've only met briefly.

580
00:49:16,040 --> 00:49:19,480
We haven't had a chance to talk yet.
We'll see each other more often now.

581
00:49:20,280 --> 00:49:21,440
Right, Wee?

582
00:49:23,720 --> 00:49:24,840
Yes.

583
00:49:27,240 --> 00:49:28,440
Wait a minute.

584
00:49:30,040 --> 00:49:31,440
You two are brothers?

585
00:49:32,040 --> 00:49:33,680
Oh.

586
00:49:34,320 --> 00:49:36,040
Alyssa, you didn't know?

587
00:49:37,280 --> 00:49:40,080
What kind of boyfriend are you, Korn?

588
00:49:40,160 --> 00:49:42,200
Why didn't you tell Alyssa?

589
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:45,680
Rawee and Phakorn grew up together.

590
00:49:47,080 --> 00:49:49,800
Phakorn was adopted by Rawee's family.

591
00:49:52,520 --> 00:49:54,680
You're Aunt Walai's adopted son?

592
00:49:56,280 --> 00:49:57,800
You know my mother?

593
00:50:00,920 --> 00:50:03,200
I mean my adoptive mother.

594
00:50:08,360 --> 00:50:10,600
You already know Rawee, don't you, Alyssa?

595
00:50:12,400 --> 00:50:13,520
Yes.

596
00:50:13,600 --> 00:50:16,400
Mr. Rawee once saved my life.

597
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:19,160
And he also works with my father.

598
00:50:19,880 --> 00:50:23,640
That's right.
I brought Rawee over from Mr. Nimit.

599
00:50:25,960 --> 00:50:28,440
Excuse me.
I'll go pick up the flowers first.

600
00:50:32,040 --> 00:50:35,200
Ms. Nada, you can get ready
to go on stage now.

601
00:50:36,920 --> 00:50:38,080
I'll leave you all for now.

602
00:50:38,680 --> 00:50:39,640
Yes.

603
00:50:43,800 --> 00:50:44,640
Korn.

604
00:50:45,880 --> 00:50:47,000
What?

605
00:50:54,200 --> 00:50:56,520
Hello, you're…

606
00:51:00,680 --> 00:51:02,960
This is Alyssa, my girlfriend,
Uncle Panas.

607
00:51:05,400 --> 00:51:06,640
Nice to meet you.

608
00:51:07,800 --> 00:51:08,680
Nice to meet you.

609
00:51:19,640 --> 00:51:21,160
Alyssa.

610
00:51:23,000 --> 00:51:24,480
Hey, Alyssa.

611
00:51:26,680 --> 00:51:29,120
I'm sorry I didn't tell you about Wee.

612
00:51:29,200 --> 00:51:32,440
I didn't know you knew each other,
so I didn't say anything.

613
00:51:33,160 --> 00:51:35,040
I'm not upset about that.

614
00:51:35,120 --> 00:51:36,680
I'm here today

615
00:51:36,760 --> 00:51:39,720
as your friend
and as a partner of Tayawat Group.

616
00:51:40,400 --> 00:51:41,800
We talked about this, Korn.

617
00:51:42,440 --> 00:51:45,880
If I knew you'd introduce me
as your girlfriend, I wouldn't have come.

618
00:51:47,360 --> 00:51:50,000
Wee! The flowers!

619
00:51:50,080 --> 00:51:51,720
I'll take them. Give them here.

620
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:54,400
Wee.

621
00:51:58,360 --> 00:51:59,320
I'll be right back.

622
00:52:02,120 --> 00:52:03,440
I need to talk to you.

623
00:52:14,560 --> 00:52:17,360
Thank you all for honoring us
by joining us today.

624
00:52:17,440 --> 00:52:19,520
Let's take a look together

625
00:52:19,600 --> 00:52:22,480
at how the TWG Wellness Residence project

626
00:52:22,560 --> 00:52:25,520
meets the needs of our aging society.

627
00:52:45,120 --> 00:52:47,120
I didn't know
you and Alyssa knew each other.

628
00:52:48,320 --> 00:52:50,720
Alyssa is the person I saved
when I got shot.

629
00:52:52,760 --> 00:52:54,320
I did talk to her,

630
00:52:55,480 --> 00:52:57,640
but I never told her about our family.

631
00:53:00,640 --> 00:53:02,360
-I just--
-Why did you decide

632
00:53:02,440 --> 00:53:04,120
to work at the same place as me?

633
00:53:05,400 --> 00:53:06,840
I didn't want to come either.

634
00:53:07,680 --> 00:53:11,400
It was Ms. Nada
who personally asked me to join.

635
00:53:30,080 --> 00:53:32,040
Are you still upset with me, Alyssa?

636
00:53:35,400 --> 00:53:36,800
I'm sorry.

637
00:53:36,880 --> 00:53:39,320
I rushed things.

638
00:53:40,240 --> 00:53:43,800
Honestly, after we met at the library,

639
00:53:44,600 --> 00:53:46,920
I never thought we'd meet again.

640
00:53:49,360 --> 00:53:51,600
But when I got the chance
to see you again,

641
00:53:51,680 --> 00:53:54,080
I promised myself

642
00:53:54,160 --> 00:53:56,480
I wouldn't look at anyone but you.

643
00:54:01,200 --> 00:54:03,360
I thought we agreed to take things slow.

644
00:54:03,440 --> 00:54:06,520
I know. I just…

645
00:54:06,600 --> 00:54:08,600
I got too caught up in my feelings.

646
00:54:10,360 --> 00:54:11,640
Thank you for bringing me home.

647
00:54:11,720 --> 00:54:13,120
Alyssa.

648
00:54:14,320 --> 00:54:17,360
You're not going to stop seeing me, right?

649
00:54:19,360 --> 00:54:21,720
Just don't do something like this again.

650
00:54:23,280 --> 00:54:26,440
Then after we finish
our meeting with my mother,

651
00:54:26,520 --> 00:54:27,840
let's go get something to eat.

652
00:54:29,680 --> 00:54:31,240
Drive safely.

653
00:54:32,720 --> 00:54:34,320
See you at the office.

654
00:55:10,200 --> 00:55:11,960
Did you want to talk?

655
00:55:13,680 --> 00:55:14,880
I'm just surprised

656
00:55:14,960 --> 00:55:17,920
by everything I learned today.

657
00:55:19,240 --> 00:55:21,480
I didn't think the world was this small.

658
00:55:23,240 --> 00:55:25,640
I see. And?

659
00:55:28,880 --> 00:55:30,800
It can get even smaller.

660
00:55:31,400 --> 00:55:34,440
I'm going to become a partner
with Tayawat Group.

661
00:55:35,800 --> 00:55:37,920
Looks like we'll be seeing each other
more often.

662
00:55:38,480 --> 00:55:40,280
Both at home and at work.

663
00:55:56,440 --> 00:55:57,520
INTERVIEW WITH HANDSOME VP PHAKORN,

664
00:55:57,600 --> 00:56:01,080
THE MAN SHAPING TAYAWAT GROUP'S
10-BILLION-BAHT BRAND

665
00:56:01,160 --> 00:56:02,760
MOM

666
00:56:04,800 --> 00:56:07,320
Korn started his first project, Mom.

667
00:56:07,400 --> 00:56:09,680
He really looks like an executive.

668
00:56:19,040 --> 00:56:22,320
If you become my secretary,
then who will help Mom?

669
00:56:23,160 --> 00:56:26,000
I'll handle both roles.

670
00:56:26,600 --> 00:56:28,360
But don't worry, Mr. Phakorn.

671
00:56:28,440 --> 00:56:30,520
In the meantime, I'll train someone new.

672
00:56:30,600 --> 00:56:34,000
Ms. Nada
will definitely have an assistant.

673
00:56:34,080 --> 00:56:35,080
Here.

674
00:56:47,120 --> 00:56:48,520
Rawee, right?

675
00:56:49,480 --> 00:56:50,320
Yes.

676
00:56:50,400 --> 00:56:53,240
Once Wee is fully trained,

677
00:56:53,320 --> 00:56:55,240
Ms. Nada
will probably make him her assistant.

678
00:56:55,320 --> 00:56:59,080
Then I'll become your full-time secretary,
Mr. Phakorn.

679
00:57:20,240 --> 00:57:21,360
Korn.

680
00:57:21,920 --> 00:57:24,320
Are you happy
with having a secretary to help you?

681
00:57:25,160 --> 00:57:28,000
Yes, I am. But…

682
00:57:29,600 --> 00:57:30,800
Is something wrong?

683
00:57:35,520 --> 00:57:37,720
We really do keep running into each other.

684
00:57:42,120 --> 00:57:42,960
Yes.

685
00:57:44,320 --> 00:57:45,240
Well…

686
00:57:46,560 --> 00:57:50,160
Could I switch Ms. Taddao with Wee?

687
00:58:15,440 --> 00:58:19,200
I'm warning you. Stay away from Ms. Nada.

688
00:58:20,640 --> 00:58:22,400
I have something for you.

689
00:58:22,480 --> 00:58:24,560
Hey, no.

690
00:58:24,640 --> 00:58:27,520
I'm not giving you the car.
I want you to drive me.

691
00:58:27,600 --> 00:58:29,120
<i>Why does Nada care so much</i>

692
00:58:29,200 --> 00:58:31,600
<i>about that kid?</i>

693
00:58:31,680 --> 00:58:33,800
The kid whose name sounds like Rawich's?

694
00:58:33,880 --> 00:58:35,880
He even looks similar.

695
00:58:36,520 --> 00:58:38,240
Now this is getting interesting.

696
00:58:38,320 --> 00:58:42,040
I'd like to have Rawee,
my new assistant, join the meeting.

697
00:58:42,720 --> 00:58:43,920
Rawee?

698
00:58:45,400 --> 00:58:47,720
<i>Maybe this place</i>
<i>suits you more than me, Wee.</i>

699
00:58:47,800 --> 00:58:49,760
What exactly do you want, Korn?

700
00:58:50,360 --> 00:58:53,320
<i>Do you want to tell the truth,</i>
<i>or keep things this way?</i>

701
00:58:53,400 --> 00:58:54,520
So I'll know what to do.

702
00:58:55,320 --> 00:58:57,360
<i>Thank you for making me realize</i>

703
00:58:57,440 --> 00:58:59,600
<i>that I still matter to you.</i>

704
00:58:59,680 --> 00:59:01,360
<i>But I'm afraid</i>

705
00:59:01,440 --> 00:59:04,560
<i>you'll find someone better than me.</i>

706
00:59:41,760 --> 00:59:44,280
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
